; USBCDC.INF - Windows 2000 to 8, x86 and x64: binds Windows' own usbser.sys
; to CDC-ACM functions as COM ports (docs/design/serial.md 5.3). Original
; INF; Windows supplies every binary. Unsigned, no catalog (build.md 7).
[Version]
Signature="$Windows NT$"
Class=Ports
ClassGuid={4D36E978-E325-11CE-BFC1-08002BE10318}
Provider=%Provider%
DriverVer=10/26/2026,0.1.3.0

[Manufacturer]
%Provider%=Models,NTx86,NTamd64

; Model sections generated by geninf.ps1 from boardids.txt.
; Windows 2000: listed whole devices (a composite board loses its other
; functions; Owner, 2026-10-20, Q5) and, as on XP, the CDC-ACM function
; class for a function a bus splits off: no in-box INF binds it (Owner,
; 2026-10-26; serial.md 5.4). The USBCOM\ id is for manual "Have Disk"
; selection only: no device reports it (Owner, 2026-10-22).
